ing that the number 4 is included in the resulting range.  Conversely, the =
right line, labeled `excl. 4` in orange, points to a node labeled `[]`, sig=
nifying that the number 4 is excluded from the resulting range on that side=
.  The arrows indicate the direction of the range operation, showing how th=
e input range is processed to produce two distinct output ranges based on i=
nclusion or exclusion of the value 4." loading=3D"lazy" width=3D"348" heigh=
